  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Introducing a dual-phase microstructure containing a ductile matrix and coherent lamellar precipitates or particles can concurrently improve strength and ductility in a W-based refractory high-entropy alloy.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::chunk::003::discussion::98e65aafcb"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The initial W-based refractory high-entropy alloy is conventionally single-phase or coarse-grained and lacks engineered microstructural features.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Controlled annealing or heat treatment can form the proposed dual-phase structure with coherent δ-lamellae and fine γ″ particles.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The engineered W-based alloy contains coherent δ-lamellae and γ″ particles within an fcc matrix.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::chunk::003::discussion::98e65aafcb"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed deformation mechanism operates during room-temperature tensile deformation.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::chunk::003::discussion::98e65aafcb"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The concurrent strength–ductility improvement may also operate at elevated temperatures.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Coherent δ-lamellae interact with dislocations during tensile deformation.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::chunk::003::discussion::98e65aafcb"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The coherent lamellae are uniformly distributed throughout a ductile matrix.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dislocations are initially pinned by the coherent δ-lamellae, thereby increasing strength.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "As strain increases, dislocation slip bands shear the coherent δ-lamellae.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::chunk::003::discussion::98e65aafcb"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Shearing of the δ-lamellae alleviates local stress concentration rather than creating a crack.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::chunk::003::discussion::98e65aafcb"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The δ-lamellae undergo strain-induced re-orientation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lamella shearing or re-orientation activates transformation-induced plasticity.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stress-concentration relief and transformation-induced plasticity improve ductility.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::chunk::003::discussion::98e65aafcb"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to a homogeneous W-based alloy, the treated alloy will have both higher yield strength and greater ductility.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::chunk::003::discussion::98e65aafcb",
        "PMC4145285::chunk::002::discussion::f8c841f9e4"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "A fine lamellar fcc/B2 structure can provide a balance of high fracture strength and high ductility in a eutectic high-entropy alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC4145285::chunk::002::discussion::f8c841f9e4"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Maintaining coherent, well-distributed lamellae is necessary for the concurrent improvement.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Loss of precipitate coherency can prevent concurrent strength and ductility improvement.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Non-optimal phase spacing can prevent concurrent strength and ductility improvement.",
      "field": "boundary",
